From 9c61f820aed266da641379631edc4317dd2744e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 08:35:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] chronik: native V2 service host wiring

Run the native V2 service on Lotus V2 nodes as an OwnEnv extension driven
after the core, porting the V2 parts of chronik-lib bridge.rs and
chronik-cpp get_v2_binding/bridge_v2_native_block:

- ConvertV2NativeBlock: 134-byte header with parent ID and height patched
  in, V2 transactions re-encoded with the default profile (coinbase and
  inputs normalized like the Rust bridge), explorer facts, native outputs.
- Open: <indexes>/chronik/v2_index, fresh when wiped or without mdbx.dat,
  reopened fresh if opening fails; the previous service is released first.
- Resync (after the core's): pop checkpoints off the active chain, replay
  the active chain, stop at the first error, publish the authority.
- Connect/Disconnect: read the block from disk (the core's Block carries no
  node block), publish the authority after success; failures are logged
  and never fail the legacy indexer.

The v2_index env is MDBX, so the service is built only with the MDBX
backend (CHRONIK_NATIVE_HAVE_LOTUS_V2_SERVICE); LevelDB-only builds keep
the V2 groups of the legacy index without the V2 service.

Tier: V2

Coordinator integration provenance (network403):
Resolve integration context by retaining the incoming purposeful change together with existing shared/native consumers; exact old/new patch and file inventory is retained in owner-adaptations.json. No authored purpose or removed downstream behavior restored.
Original scripted commands/hashes above are original-author provenance; modified parent/tool/catalog hashes are not claimed to reproduce this composition. Exact coordinator adaptation scripts and ordered tree proof are in composed403-network-metrics-delivery. Build/runtime/benchmarks NOT_RUN for this composition under user compile-first policy.

